@ProfNoahGian @skdh 100%. 

most of what’s going right now is that you can use Lean (a symbolic tool!) to verify problems that can be formalized, and there is genuine progress there. But the real world is complicated and mostly resists that level of formalization, and the current techniques don’t work as well there.

This matters a LOT, because many people are extrapolating, incorrectly in my view, from progress on a certain class of math problems (which is real) to progress on AGI and science in general (much less clear).

@ChrSzegedy Thanks for sharing! Not sure if I believe all the same, but I can also see a similar bifurcation into "immediately useful math" and "understanding-driven math".

From the outside I'd be surprised if costs stay so high. But maybe we get really ambitious
